From cf4d62d555f4458af016fd27affc540e93cbacc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiveManQuestion <>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:14:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep running RSP tasks that return without halting

When the RSP plugin returns from doRspCycles without the task halting or
breaking (cxd4 does this when the microcode polls SP_STATUS for the CPU),
do_SP_Task marks the task locked and queues an SP interrupt event, but the
task only ran again when the CPU wrote SP_STATUS. Pokemon Stadium 2's GB
Tower leaves its RSP task running and never writes SP_STATUS again, so it
hung on a black screen after loading the Game Boy cartridge. Resume the
task from the SP interrupt event instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/device/rcp/rsp/rsp_core.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/device/rcp/rsp/rsp_core.c b/src/device/rcp/rsp/rsp_core.c
index 99767bc0..05956565 100644
--- a/src/device/rcp/rsp/rsp_core.c
+++ b/src/device/rcp/rsp/rsp_core.c
@@ -406,6 +406,17 @@ void rsp_interrupt_event(void* opaque)
 {
     struct rsp_core* sp = (struct rsp_core*)opaque;
 
+    /* The RSP plugin returned without the task halting or breaking (cxd4
+     * does this when the microcode polls SP_STATUS waiting for the CPU).
+     * Keep running the task instead of waiting for the CPU to write
+     * SP_STATUS: Pokemon Stadium 2's GB Tower leaves its RSP task running
+     * and never writes SP_STATUS again, so it hung on a black screen. */
+    if (sp->rsp_task_locked && !(sp->regs[SP_STATUS_REG] & (SP_STATUS_HALT | SP_STATUS_BROKE)))
+    {
+        do_SP_Task(sp);
+        return;
+    }
+
     if (!sp->rsp_task_locked)
     {
         sp->regs[SP_STATUS_REG] |=
